# gap12-apply-command: full wire command surface + state CRC

## Plan premise (stale) vs reality

The plan row assumed "~17 Command variants; 11 lack arms" and asked for a state CRC
beside the command hash. Recon showed both already exist:

- All 17 `Command` variants (network.rs ~62-78) have explicit arms in
  `Game::try_apply_command` (game.rs:2939+), and the match has NO catch-all, so a
  future variant fails to compile. `apply_command` (:2933) wraps it with the
  historical `bool` return for replay/UI callers.
- A deterministic FNV-1a 64-bit state CRC exists: `Game::state_crc()`
  (game.rs:3129) over `to_save_bytes()`, recorded per executed frame in
  `LockstepSession` (state_crcs at :469).

So the deliverable reduced to the plan's NAMED acceptance tests, written here.

## Variant-by-variant verification (via the new test)

| Variant | Arm | Test asserts |
|---|---|---|
| Move | order_units_move | path queued |
| Attack | order_units_attack | arm returns true, target latched |
| Stop | order_units_stop | ordered cleared |
| Guard | target + ordered | target latched |
| Build | queue_building + place_ready_building | enqueues (owned yard) |
| Sell | sell_building | building down + refund credits |
| Repair | repair_building | applies on damaged owned building |
| Power | set_powered | is_powered flipped |
| Produce | queue_unit | enqueues (barracks) |
| Deploy | deployed = true | flag flipped |
| Undeploy | deployed = false | flag flipped |
| Sabotage | network::apply_sabotage | applies (commando vs enemy bldg) |
| RepairStructure | repair_building | applies (damaged owned bldg) |
| CancelProduction | cancel_production | applies on a queued item |
| PlaceBuilding | place_ready_building | buildings.len() + 1 |
| Board | apply_board -> load_transport_at | applies (APC + friendly pax) |
| Unload | apply_unload -> unload_transport_at | applies (loaded APC) |

## Tests added (TDD; each observed failing first)

- `every_command_variant_applies` — drives all 17 variants through
  `apply_command` on a live populated game and asserts the observable state change
  each arm promises. Discovered gates while writing it (all real engine contracts,
  now pinned): repair needs credits AND a damaged building; sabotage needs a
  commando reaching an enemy building; Board/Unload need a transport with friendly
  passengers; PlaceBuilding places only the front COMPLETED structure;
  CancelProduction needs a queued item.
- `state_crc_detects_divergence` — two games given the same command stream share
  `state_crc()`; one extra command on one game makes the CRCs diverge.

